ay only be accessed with my consent or for certain permissible purposes. Unauthorized credit inquiries have been made by companies I do not recognize or have not authorized.

Section 611 of the FCRA mandates that credit reporting agencies investigate disputes in a timely manner ( within 30 days ) and correct any inaccuracies. Despite my attempts to dispute these fraudulent accounts and inquiries, they remain unresolved.

Section 605A of the FCRA allows consumers to place fraud alerts or credit freezes to prevent further unauthorized access to their credit reports. I have taken these actions, but the fraudulent information continues to persist.

