Additionally, FCRA 611 requires Experian to reinvestigate disputes and remove information that can not be verified as accurate. Given that these accounts were opened as a result of identity theft, they can not be verified as legitimate accounts of mine. In fact, Ive informed Experian that the creditors themselves should have records indicating fraud ( for example, Ive informed XXXX XXXX XXXX and XXXX of the identity theft, and they flagged the accounts as fraudulent on their end ). Experian, however, appears to have conducted no meaningful investigation. This behavior aligns with the CFPBs recent allegations that Experian has been conducting sham investigations of consumer disputes simply parroting whatever the furnisher responds with, or ignoring the identity theft report, rather than investigating properly. Experians failure to remove these accounts is unlawful and has persisted even after the CFPBs enforcement action announced XX/XX/XXXX, which explicitly cites Experians failure to properly process identity theft disputes CFPB Enforcement Action Reference : I want to highlight that the CFPB sued Experian on XX/XX/XXXX for exactly this kind of behavior unlawfully failing to properly investigate consumer disputes, resulting in inaccurate information staying on reports. In that action ( Case CFPB v. Experian Information Solutions , Inc. ), the Bureau alleges Experian violated FCRA by not deleting information that was false or not verifiable and by conducting inadequate investigations. My case is a textbook example of Experians misconduct : despite being presented with a valid identity theft report ( which under law should immediately trigger blocking of the fraudulent data ) Experian has left the data on my report for nearly a year. This shows willful non-compliance or gross negligence on Experians part. 

Harm to Me : Experians failure to remove the fraudulent accounts has caused significant harm : My credit score has plummeted due to the derogatory items ( charge-off, collection, large auto debt ). This has caused me to be denied legitimate credit and caused emotional distress.

I spend countless hours repeatedly disputing and monitoring my credit, which is a burden. 
The presence of the fraudulent accounts delays my ability to rebuild my credit ; I can not get accurate credit until Experian removes them. 

Desired Resolution : I am filing this complaint to seek the CFPBs assistance in forcing Experian to comply with the law. I request the CFPB to : 1. Order Experian to immediately block and remove all fraudulent accounts and inquiries from my credit report pursuant to FCRA 605B.

2. Ensure Experian updates my credit file and provides me a corrected report with those items deleted, so I can move forward.

3. Consider this complaint as further evidence in the CFPBs enforcement action Experians continued flouting of FCRA even after the lawsuit was filed.

4. Impose any appropriate penalties for Experians failure to comply with FCRA 605B and 611 in my case. 

I have attached documentation supporting my case : copies of my credit report highlighting the fraudulent items, my FTC Identity Theft Report, and letters Ive sent to Experian ( with proof of receipt ). I am happy to provide any additional information the CFPB needs. My goal is simply to have my credit report corrected and to prevent Experian from harming other identity theft victims in this manner. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this complaint. Experians negligent handling of clear-cut identity theft is unacceptable, and I trust the CFPB will help enforce my rights under the FCRA and FACTA. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, NV XXXX ( XXXX ) XXXX | XXXX XXXX",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NV,89103,,Web,2025-04-07,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
