12860385,2025-04-07,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"Subject : Dispute of Fraudulent Accounts on Credit Reports Due to Data Breaches Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to formally dispute two unauthorized accounts appearing on my credit reports from XXXX, XXXXransUnion, and Equifax. As a XXXX individual who no longer drives and manages finances on a fixed income, I have never applied for or obtained an auto loan or a credit card. I recently received notifications that my personal information was compromised in multiple data breaches, including those involving Equifax, XXXX XXXXXXXX and XXXX XXXX and XXXX, and the XXXX XXXX XXXX. I believe these breaches have led to identity theft, resulting in the following fraudulent accounts being reported on my credit reports : XXXX XXXXl : XXXX XXXX  for {$19000.00} XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX with a balance of {$2000.00} These accounts are clearly fraudulent, as I have never applied for them. The presence of these unauthorized accounts violates several consumer protection laws : 1. 18 U.S.C. 1028A Aggravated Identity Theft : This statute imposes severe penalties for knowingly transferring, possessing, or using, without lawful authority, a means of identification of another person. The existence of these accounts indicates that my identity has been unlawfully used.

